{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 802 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "70339f6023ab4a6f7d7afa401d5d9f2c829981bd361094eb8908bd636e5b38c6" :edb/db-before-t 801 :edb/db-after-t 802 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534114 50 #inst "2026-10-06T03:13:33.923Z" 13194139534114 true] [17592186059604 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277703 13194139534114 true] [17592186059770 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277713 13194139534114 true] [17592186059788 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277668 13194139534114 true] [17592186068620 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277661 13194139534114 true] [17592186069252 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534114 true] [17592186069252 1100 "Simplify $\\frac{5 + b}{3b} + \\frac{6 - b}{3b}$." 13194139534114 false] [17592186069252 1100 "Simplify $\\frac{5+b}{3b}+\\frac{6-b}{3b}.$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186069252 1145 "We have a common denominator of $3b,$ so we add the numerators and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5+b}{3b}+\\frac{6-b}{3b} & = \\\\ \\frac{5+b+6-b}{3b} & = \\\\ \\frac{(5+6)+(b-b)}{3b} & = \\\\ \\frac{11}{3b}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186073754 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277710 13194139534114 true] [17592186083246 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277689 13194139534114 true] [17592186087769 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277675 13194139534114 true] [17592186129652 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534114 true] [17592186129652 1100 "Given that $(x + 3)$ is a factor of $f(x) = 2x^{3} + 8x^{2} + 7x + 3$, which of the following curves is generated by $y = f(x)$?\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" 13194139534114 false] [17592186129652 1100 "Given that $(x+3)$ is a factor of $f(x)=2{x}^{3}+8{x}^{2}+7x+3,$ which of the following curves is generated by $y=f(x)?$\n\n(*Note: Figures not drawn to scale*)" 13194139534114 true] [17592186129652 1145 "First, we need to factor the polynomial. We are told that $(x+3)$ is a factor of $f(x),$ so $(x+3)$ divides $f(x)$ with zero remainder. To begin factoring $f(x),$ we can divide it by $(x+3)$ using synthetic division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {x}^{3} & {x}^{2} & {x}^{1} & {x}^{0} \\\\ -3 & 2 & 8 & 7 & 3 \\\\  &  & -6 & -6 & -3 \\\\  & 2 & 2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{f(x)}{x+3}=2{x}^{2}+2x+1\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\nf(x)=(x+3)(2{x}^{2}+2x+1).\n$$\n\nThe equation is now fully factored. Note that the discriminant of $2{x}^{2}+2x+1=0$ is \n\n$$\nD=(2)^{2}-4(2)(1)=-4<0,\n$$\n\nwhich implies that the quadratic factor has no real roots. So by the zero-product rule, we deduce that $f(x)$ has a single root at $x=-3.$ \n\nWe also find the $y$-intercept of the curve by substituting the value $x=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2(0)^{3}+8(0)^{2}+7(0)+3=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the curve:\n\n- has a $y$-intercept at $(0,3),$\n\n- passes through the $x$-axis at the single root $x=-3,$ and\n\n- has no more $x$-intercepts.\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the graph takes an inverted $\\text{S}$-shape. Therefore, the graph looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975009/assets/f004d901b5738a46732f41c12f12c812432a2fa14af71469b5abff49e368607d.png)" 13194139534114 true] [17592186184099 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277682 13194139534114 true] [17592186192639 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277696 13194139534114 true] [17592186277661 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277662 13194139534114 true] [17592186277661 1089 "q-104040" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277661 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534114 true] [17592186277661 1100 "Select the function that has a discontinuity at $x=-3.$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277661 1113 #uuid "26714345-59e1-5173-b792-dc1a82d81e99" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277661 1145 "The correct answer is shown below. Notice that the function contains a break exactly at $x=-3$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nAll the other given graphs can be plotted without taking the pencil off of the paper." 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277663 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277664 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277665 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277666 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277667 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1041 "selection" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277664 13194139534114 true] [17592186277662 1110 #uuid "9bd3b028-ad15-58f6-ac93-8b4d97f1b096" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277663 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975009/assets/701e652c0db6997cae3fe82828cfe37a7dd4ddb07712fb0dd2b747f47b94a3d0.png" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277663 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534114 true] [17592186277663 1111 #uuid "3b3d0655-2605-5ced-82b9-6b1c4a94930d" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277664 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975009/assets/deacb7f7b36ae12e236a3d5eae46def61ba2570a2cd8d7a4bb4527ce9d2cec7b.png" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277664 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534114 true] [17592186277664 1111 #uuid "7531a2d4-2ea7-5994-8aa7-7ea6bd35d471" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277665 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975009/assets/a3026fef480f96f0b1d1583c0136b3b7c82054bbce13b2480a14fa37cba608f6.png" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277665 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534114 true] [17592186277665 1111 #uuid "ccdb4c6f-4f60-534a-9181-df0c5e161fa7" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277666 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975009/assets/9eb01437ae94e15e061548f8be50dfd101d5350fb3550a131afe7ff5fd975c10.png" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277666 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534114 true] [17592186277666 1111 #uuid "b8b33720-8474-5f76-9f5e-a0e306fa7933" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277667 1034 "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975009/assets/e56e3c7e64c1bfa06b48a00225f3b7cf0551397ab96d160c88989ea24b70584b.png" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277667 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045452 13194139534114 true] [17592186277667 1111 #uuid "c38935c7-e9aa-5754-8a68-cbe8f76a0ca7" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277668 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277669 13194139534114 true] [17592186277668 1089 "q-10735" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277668 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534114 true] [17592186277668 1100 "If $y=-\\frac{3}{{x}^{7}},$ find $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277668 1113 #uuid "778ca374-f002-5bcc-9db6-f0d4476b5986" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277668 1145 "We first rewrite the function as\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{{x}^{7}}=-3{x}^{-7}.\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the constant multiple and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{x}^{-7}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-7}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (-7){x}^{-7-1} \\\\  & =21{x}^{-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{{x}^{8}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277670 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277671 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277672 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277673 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277674 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1041 "selection" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277674 13194139534114 true] [17592186277669 1110 #uuid "a2eabba0-4025-511f-8464-843dab99c26d" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277670 1034 "21{x}^{7}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277670 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277670 1111 #uuid "4420dc69-ff6f-5e56-b4be-9ab9823215d4" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277671 1034 "18{x}^{5}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277671 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277671 1111 #uuid "07fd0db0-b5f5-5a3d-9284-594cd72e2ba0" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277672 1034 "\\frac{21}{{x}^{-8}}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277672 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277672 1111 #uuid "fdbc4307-6880-58c1-80a5-04acdd3cd7b2" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277673 1034 "-\\frac{21}{{x}^{8}}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277673 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277673 1111 #uuid "ae62b9fd-68a3-5e20-9ced-38c37543f946" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277674 1034 "\\frac{21}{{x}^{8}}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277674 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277674 1111 #uuid "326b8b90-9f9b-5434-af6a-87598a59f30d" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277675 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277676 13194139534114 true] [17592186277675 1089 "q-113253" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277675 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534114 true] [17592186277675 1100 "What are the solutions of the equation $(x-1)^{2}=-64?$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277675 1113 #uuid "84fcd074-662f-5f90-a82a-a4386fd75d95" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277675 1145 "The left-hand side is a perfect square. Therefore, we can solve the equation using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2} & =-64 \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{-64} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 8\\,\\text{i} \\\\ x & =1\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation has two solutions, $x=1+8\\,\\text{i}$ and $x=1-8\\,\\text{i}.$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277677 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277678 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277679 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277680 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277681 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1041 "selection" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277679 13194139534114 true] [17592186277676 1110 #uuid "445f5743-6ad5-5ff8-861d-7e4659223e30" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277677 1034 "x=8\\pm \\text{i}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277677 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277677 1111 #uuid "df06f99b-147c-5282-bd87-037367f5e317" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277678 1034 "x=-1\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277678 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277678 1111 #uuid "0f54602d-b2e5-5568-b875-11ddb4a5298a" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277679 1034 "x=1\\pm 8\\,\\text{i}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277679 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277679 1111 #uuid "f4148326-16bb-596c-b7d2-7961bfd1c4d6" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277680 1034 "x=8\\pm 16\\,\\text{i}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277680 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277680 1111 #uuid "91807a7b-5577-51b7-8ce5-db0475ab0616" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277681 1034 "x=1\\pm 64\\,\\text{i}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277681 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277681 1111 #uuid "3755fa66-a91c-5660-95ca-d899725aa273" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277682 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277683 13194139534114 true] [17592186277682 1089 "q-113848" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277682 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534114 true] [17592186277682 1100 "Find the antiderivative of \n$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}+{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277682 1113 #uuid "de0205fc-51f4-5abe-9cd4-dc41ea4ca473" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277682 1145 "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}+{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-4/3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x-\\int {x}^{-2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4/3+1}}{(-\\frac{4}{3}+1)}+\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{(3+1)}-\\frac{{x}^{-2+1}}{(-2+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/3}}{(-\\frac{1}{3})}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{(-1)}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{1}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277684 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277685 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277686 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277687 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277688 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1041 "selection" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277687 13194139534114 true] [17592186277683 1110 #uuid "ed0c53a3-4019-58e4-9a40-c36428ea9886" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277684 1034 "\\sqrt[3]{x}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{x}{4}+C" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277684 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277684 1111 #uuid "e556c0f3-37ea-5971-9b0b-d264db36d7d4" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277685 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}{3}+4{x}^{4}+\\frac{x}{2}+C" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277685 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277685 1111 #uuid "a1d7e7bf-98d4-5aff-b255-91863d5b5f7e" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277686 1034 "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}+C" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277686 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277686 1111 #uuid "fe127715-e44c-5723-a4a4-0f5c6e3ec150" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277687 1034 "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{1}{x}+C" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277687 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277687 1111 #uuid "3dc36b19-ff15-5d50-9511-e6c8a3296f86" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277688 1034 "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{4}}}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{1}{x}+C" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277688 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277688 1111 #uuid "56e78c2c-10d9-5bab-8e1b-fda29a511635" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277689 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277690 13194139534114 true] [17592186277689 1089 "q-124410" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277689 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534114 true] [17592186277689 1100 "$3!-0!=$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277689 1113 #uuid "df44a4f2-8e7b-5965-860a-aa02ef9d22dd" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277689 1145 "The given expression is a subtraction of two factorials.\n\n- Computing $3!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n3!=3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=6.\n$$\n\n- By definition, the factorial of zero equals one:\n\n$$\n0!=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3!-0! & =6-1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277691 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277692 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277693 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277694 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277695 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1041 "selection" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277695 13194139534114 true] [17592186277690 1110 #uuid "80641b3f-2dcc-5305-b6a8-37de7514ac53" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277691 1034 "8" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277691 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277691 1111 #uuid "667ff609-a8e0-5d1d-a1c2-413c93c19b2c" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277692 1034 "2" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277692 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277692 1111 #uuid "f689fae0-046f-5964-834f-fbab504d1230" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277693 1034 "6" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277693 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277693 1111 #uuid "2f111851-8eee-5065-b7ab-916fa003e91a" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277694 1034 "Undefined" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277694 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534114 true] [17592186277694 1111 #uuid "cc747dbe-0407-5d0a-82a3-da3f8e721368" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277695 1034 "5" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277695 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277695 1111 #uuid "4020eecd-7361-56e5-9f4e-d5bea4e9152d" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277696 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277697 13194139534114 true] [17592186277696 1089 "q-148444" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277696 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534114 true] [17592186277696 1100 "The function $f(x)=\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{2}}$ is defined for $x>-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find ${f}^{-1}(x).$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277696 1113 #uuid "f7c93dc9-ef3f-57a5-9461-a74860dab0b0" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277696 1145 "To find ${f}^{-1}(x),$ we start by replacing $f(x)$ with $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, interchanging $x$ and $y$ gives\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{(2y+1)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we make $y$ the subject of the equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{(2y+1)^{2}} \\\\ (2y+1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ \\sqrt{(2y+1)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{x}} \\\\ |2y+1| & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 2y+1 & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ 2y & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-1 \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the fact that for $y>-\\frac{1}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n|2y+1|=2y+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse function is \n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277698 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277699 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277700 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277701 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277702 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1041 "selection" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277701 13194139534114 true] [17592186277697 1110 #uuid "db7c514e-4f1f-5758-b45b-4a45a7dffe70" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277698 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277698 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277698 1111 #uuid "ad1d944f-7079-5621-b71b-8dae7c7b7e98" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277699 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-2" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277699 1111 #uuid "8116fb68-2f6f-5fdd-b2c2-4e3bd521beef" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277700 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}+1" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277700 1111 #uuid "bd9c30c7-ffc9-577d-b271-e8743c0b6134" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277701 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277701 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277701 1111 #uuid "a490c015-c11f-50e9-af4f-eeae6c6ee767" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277702 1034 "{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}-1" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277702 1111 #uuid "d0a5d34e-c140-5220-82c7-577bf52de87d" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277703 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277704 13194139534114 true] [17592186277703 1089 "q-22978" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277703 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534114 true] [17592186277703 1100 "Which angle is coterminal with $-{175}^{∘}?$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277703 1113 #uuid "5d8dcd0b-e0c8-5bbf-9e83-e01bcc550fb1" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277703 1145 "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $ (in degrees), we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{∘}$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ to $-{175}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{175}^{∘}+{360}^{∘}={185}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{175}^{∘}+2\\cdot {360}^{∘}={545}^{∘}\\,✓$\n\nThere are no answer choices larger than ${545}^{∘},$ so we can stop here.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{∘}$ from $-{175}^{∘}$:\n\n- $-{175}^{∘}-{360}^{∘}=-{535}^{∘}$\n\n- $-{175}^{∘}-2\\cdot {360}^{∘}=-{895}^{∘}$\n\nThere are no answer choices smaller than $-{895}^{∘},$ so we can stop here.\n\nSo the correct answer is ${545}^{∘}.$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277705 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277706 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277707 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277708 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277709 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1041 "selection" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277708 13194139534114 true] [17592186277704 1110 #uuid "55a56d46-281d-5ec8-90d5-ba68a8ee96d1" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277705 1034 "-{505}^{∘}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277705 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277705 1111 #uuid "4ebee52c-17d2-50f9-841e-821bb635f2f0" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277706 1034 "{180}^{∘}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277706 1111 #uuid "a6874f49-c4b9-5a3c-91ee-f42730108937" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277707 1034 "{450}^{∘}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277707 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277707 1111 #uuid "e209b57b-63b3-559d-ba9c-1e542a26a85d" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277708 1034 "{545}^{∘}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277708 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277708 1111 #uuid "15926eda-7242-54ae-8ec2-ba359d102d7e" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277709 1034 "-{800}^{∘}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277709 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277709 1111 #uuid "f50dc8aa-38d8-5671-93c1-9dd4eab56638" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277710 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277711 13194139534114 true] [17592186277710 1089 "q-262221" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277710 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534114 true] [17592186277710 1100 "The distance between the points $A(3,1,2)$ and $B(5,-3,4)$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139534114 true] [17592186277710 1113 #uuid "15259eb9-e584-5617-b029-3ef6354f46e2" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277710 1145 "The distance $d$ between two points $A({x}_{1},{y}_{1},{z}_{1})$ and $B({x}_{2},{y}_{2},{z}_{2})$ is given by\n\n$$\nd=\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({z}_{2}-{z}_{1})^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $A{{(3,1,2)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{, }{y}_{1}\\text{, }{z}_{1}\\text{)}}$ and $B{{(5,-3,4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{, }{y}_{2}\\text{, }{z}_{2}\\text{)}}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{(5-3)^{2}+(-3-1)^{2}+(4-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{24} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277711 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277712 13194139534114 true] [17592186277711 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534114 true] [17592186277711 1041 "field-1" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277711 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277712 13194139534114 true] [17592186277711 1110 #uuid "3676e022-27c6-5903-8d25-f11f842f5262" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277712 1034 "2\\sqrt{6}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277712 1111 #uuid "f6af8c94-9bc1-5889-9a8c-de0a46a865e0" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277713 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277714 13194139534114 true] [17592186277713 1089 "q-86322" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277713 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534114 true] [17592186277713 1100 "$\\operatorname{sec}⁡{135}^{∘}=$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277713 1113 #uuid "3252a42d-5a90-5eb8-a245-7d72a6cbf420" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277713 1145 "Let's remind ourselves of the special trigonometric ratios, as given by the unit circle.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13975009/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the unit circle, we see that the angle ${135}^{∘}$ corresponds to the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}).$\n\nSince the cosine of the angle corresponds to the $x$-coordinate, we have $\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘}=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, using the fact that $\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta },$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡{135}^{∘}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{135}^{∘}}=-\\sqrt{2}.\n$$" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277715 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277716 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277717 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277718 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277719 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1041 "selection" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277718 13194139534114 true] [17592186277714 1110 #uuid "c1da4c49-433f-500b-803b-5f3a1a342c9a" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277715 1034 "\\sqrt{3}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277715 1111 #uuid "3be755e5-9744-50da-b6c2-6d219cf385ab" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277716 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277716 1111 #uuid "c811d858-4ca9-52b8-83cd-b5dffb4f26d4" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277717 1034 "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" 13194139534114 true] [17592186277717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534114 true] [17592186277717 1111 #uuid "903e6612-7286-5806-b2ff-fd846bc7285b" 13194139534114 true] [1759218